      "message": "a bit confusing... how about something like:\n\n  __get_task_comm() currently copies buf_size. This used to \n  expose an issue where if sizeof(buf) \u003e TASK_COMM_LEN, the \n  copy would read beyond the end of tsk-\u003ecomm. This was fixed \n  in 3756f6401c30 (\"exec: avoid gcc-8 warning for \n  get_task_comm\") by insisting at compile-time that \n  sizeof(buf) \u003d\u003d TASK_COMM_LEN.\n\n  This is overly restrictive since it is reasonable to allow buf\n  to be smaller than TASK_COMM_LEN. This patch loosens the \n  compile-time check to fail only if sizeof(buf) \u003e TASK_COMM_LEN.",
